WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.260
Data types should reflect meaning rather than

00:00:02.287 --> 00:00:05.662
only the way a value looks A

00:00:05.675 --> 00:00:08.702
generated identifier can use an identity column

00:00:09.625 --> 00:00:12.586
Exact monetary values are better represented with

00:00:12.599 --> 00:00:16.402
an exact numeric type Whole-number quantities use

00:00:16.428 --> 00:00:20.349
integer types General descriptive text can use

00:00:20.375 --> 00:00:23.823
text Birth dates use date while real-world

00:00:23.849 --> 00:00:25.967
moments such as appointment times often use

00:00:25.994 --> 00:00:30.291
timestamp with time zone Boolean is appropriate

00:00:30.318 --> 00:00:35.088
for genuinely true-or-false states Throughout this
course

00:00:35.259 --> 00:00:38.114
we also use common PostgreSQL style conventions

00:00:38.351 --> 00:00:40.943
uppercase SQL keywords lower snake case for

00:00:40.969 --> 00:00:43.325
table and column names and identity columns

00:00:43.351 --> 00:00:48.430
rather than MySQL-style AUTO_INCREMENT Do not choose

00:00:48.456 --> 00:00:50.364
a type only because a sample value

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:53.419
fits Choose the type that represents the

00:00:53.432 --> 00:00:55.222
meaning and the rules the database should

00:00:55.248 --> 00:00:55.853
enforce
